---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";

const sections = [
  ["introduction", "Introduction"],
  ["license", "License and source code"],
  ["content", "Your content and providers"],
  ["acceptable-use", "Acceptable use"],
  ["availability", "Availability and changes"],
  ["disclaimers", "Disclaimers"],
  ["liability", "Limitation of liability"],
  ["third-parties", "Third-party services"],
  ["changes", "Changes to these Terms"],
  ["contact", "Contact"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Service | Ankiel Code"
  description="The terms that govern your use of Ankiel Code, app.code.ankiel.com, and code.ankiel.com."
  heading="Ankiel Code Terms of Service"
  lede="Ankiel Code is free, MIT-licensed software that you run yourself. These Terms cover the software, the code.ankiel.com website, and the hosted web client."
  effectiveDate="2026-11-24"
  lastUpdated="2026-11-24"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="introduction">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Service (the “Terms”) govern your use of the Ankiel Code desktop, mobile, and web
      applications, the hosted web client at{" "}<a href="https://app.code.ankiel.com">https://app.code.ankiel.com</a>{" "}
      (together, the “Services”), and the website at{" "}<a href="https://code.ankiel.com">https://code.ankiel.com</a>{" "}
      (the “Site”). “We” means the maintainer of Ankiel Code. By using the Site or Services you
      agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ankiel Code is an independent fork of{" "}<a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code">T3 Code</a>, which is
      MIT licensed. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the authors of T3 Code.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="license">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>License and Source Code</h2>
    <p>
      The source code is licensed under the{" "}<a href="https://github.com/benank/ankielcode/blob/main/LICENSE"
        >MIT License</a
      >. You may use, copy, modify, and distribute it under that license. The license covers source
      code only. It does not give you the right to present a modified build as the official Ankiel Code
      release, so if you distribute a fork, make clear that it is unofficial.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="content">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>Your Content and Providers</h2>
    <p>
      You own your source code, prompts, and the output of your agents. Ankiel Code sends them only to
      the machines and providers you configure, and we do not receive them. You are responsible for
      the agents and providers you connect, for complying with their terms, and for reviewing commands
      and code changes an agent proposes before you run or apply them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="acceptable-use">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>Acceptable Use</h2>
    <p>When using the Site or Services, do not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Break the law or infringe the rights of others;</li>
      <li>Attack, probe, or overload the Site or any service we host, or try to bypass its access controls;</li>
      <li>Misrepresent an unofficial build, site, or package as official Ankiel Code.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="availability">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2>Availability and Changes</h2>
    <p>
      The Site, update feeds, and hosted web client are provided on a best-effort basis. We may change,
      suspend, or retire any of them at any time. Because Ankiel Code is self-hosted software, a copy
      you have installed keeps working without them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="disclaimers">
    <p class="section-number">06</p>
    <h2>Disclaimers</h2>
    <p>
      THE SITE AND SERVICES ARE PROVIDED “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE,” WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
      EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND
      NON-INFRINGEMENT. AI agents can make mistakes and run commands on your machine; you are
      responsible for the permissions you grant and the results you accept.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="liability">
    <p class="section-number">07</p>
    <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p>
      TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE MAINTAINER AND CONTRIBUTORS ARE NOT LIABLE FOR ANY
      INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR LOST DATA, PROFITS, OR
      REVENUE, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE SITE OR SERVICES. BECAUSE THE SOFTWARE IS FREE, OUR TOTAL
      LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM IS LIMITED TO USD $50.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-parties">
    <p class="section-number">08</p>
    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      Coding agents, AI providers, GitHub, app stores, and other services you use with Ankiel Code are
      governed by their own terms. We do not endorse or control them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <p class="section-number">09</p>
    <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms. Changes take effect when posted at this URL, and we will update the
      dates above. Continued use after a change means you accept it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <p class="section-number">10</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these Terms: open an issue at{" "}<a class="contact-link"
        href="https://github.com/benank/ankielcode/issues">github.com/benank/ankielcode/issues</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
